      "message": "@ratankgupta31@gmail.com This buffer may overflow when SHA-512 is negotiated. `libspdm_get_digest()` writes `negotiated_hash_size * popcount(slotMask)` bytes without receiving the destination capacity. Since SHA-512 is advertised, a responder reporting 7–8 slots writes 448–512 bytes into this 384-byte buffer.\nWe may allocate `LIBSPDM_MAX_HASH_SIZE * SPDM_MAX_SLOT_COUNT` and calculate totalDigestSize using the negotiated hash size rather than the fixed 48-byte value.",
